// Title: Potential Remote Desktop Tunneling
// Sigma ID: 8a3038e8-9c9d-46f8-b184-66234a160f6f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: lateral-movement, T1021
// Description: Detects potential use of an SSH utility to establish RDP over a reverse SSH Tunnel. This can be
//   used by attackers to enable routing of network packets that would otherwise not reach their
//   intended destination.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/potential-remote-desktop-tunneling-detected.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_remote_desktop_tunneling.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains ":3389" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -L " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -P " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -R " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -pw " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -ssh ")
